From 67ed269b826d92973aeac1e7936cef4eecb6ec7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Han <23090290+danielhanchen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:46:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] rpc : repack CPU matmul weights in place on the server
 (experimental)

rpc-server allocates every client buffer with the default CPU buffer type,
so the CPU extra buffer types (CPU_REPACK, AMX) never run over RPC.

With GGML_RPC_REPACK=1 (or rpc-server --repack), GRAPH_COMPUTE repacks
leaf weights that are used only as src0 of MUL_MAT / MUL_MAT_ID, in place,
with the first extra buffer type whose alloc size equals ggml_nbytes and
whose supports_op accepts every consumer. Deserialized descriptors of a
repacked weight are pointed at a view buffer of that type with
tensor->extra restored, so the CPU extra compute hook picks them up.
Cached graphs are re-pointed when the repacked set changes.

Weights seen with any other use (get_rows, views, aliasing) are never
repacked. Afterwards, a graph using a repacked weight any other way, a
GET_TENSOR / COPY_TENSOR read of it, or a partial write into it is
refused; a full overwrite drops the repack. CPU devices only, default off.

tests/test-rpc-repack.cpp: client-side checks (mixed-use weight stays
plain, matmul parity vs local CPU, re-upload, refused get/get_rows/partial
write).
